\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	11	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Rounding beneath Sublime Point.
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 After Gordon Falls the route turns south beneath the cliffs of 
\f0\b Sublime Point itself
\f1\b0 . The vegetation shifts again: more ferns in the shaded gullies, wattles and more open growth where the cliff orientation admits light. The enormous wall of Sublime Point now rises above TIGER rather than appearing as a distant destination. As they round its western side/nose, openings through the trees give them an unusual reverse view of the 
\f0\b Three Sisters behind them to the west
\f1\b0 , Mount Solitary across the valley, and the deeper country towards Kedumba beyond. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unswoc.org/wordpress/2025/07/lindeman-pass/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 UNSW OC}}\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	12	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Lindeman\'96Copeland junction.
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 There is no grand trail junction. Copeland Pass leaves Lindeman from beneath Sublime Point as a faint route, historically marked only inconsistently by cairns or ribbons. What TIGER sees is essentially a decision to stop traversing beneath the cliff and go 
\f0\b straight up into it
\f1\b0 . Above them the sandstone nose of Sublime Point rises in tiers, broken by boulders, clefts, vegetated slots and short vertical faces. The climb regains roughly 
\f0\b 270 metres of elevation in about 400 metres of horizontal travel
\f1\b0 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unswoc.org/wordpress/2025/07/lindeman-pass/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 UNSW OC}}\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	13	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Lower Copeland Pass.
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 The first ascent threads between large sandstone blocks before narrowing into a cleft where modern walkers use a fixed rope. Packs and second rifles become awkward here because passages that admit a body do not necessarily admit a body wearing a large load. Above that is a substantial rock overhang. From beneath it, the rock itself frames the Jamison Valley like a rough window: forest plunging away below, Mount Solitary across the basin, sandstone walls beyond. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hikingtheworld.blog/2023/04/14/lindeman-pass-copeland-pass/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Hiking the World}}\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	14	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The short tunnel/slot and Copeland lookout.
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 One version of the route climbs through a short rock slot or \'93tunnel\'94. Immediately above it is a small exposed sandstone platform\'97the informal 
\f0\b Copeland Pass lookout
\f1\b0 . This gives TIGER the geographically useful panorama:\
