\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	15	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Upper Copeland Pass.
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Above that platform the route attacks the cliff again. There are short near-vertical scrambles, fixed ropes on the present route, a chimney-like hole through the sandstone and exposed steps where a slip would not be arrested by vegetation. The rock is weathered Hawkesbury sandstone: ledges, rounded blocks, undercuts and iron-stained faces rather than a smooth cliff. Between scrambles the vegetation crowds back in, so the climb repeatedly alternates between enclosed slots and sudden open exposure over the valley. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mntviews.blogspot.com/2016/04/gladstone-lindeman-copeland-passes-nsw.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Mnt Views}}\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
