\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	16	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cresting onto Sublime Point.
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 The change at the top is almost comic after Copeland. The last rock scramble deposits them close to the 
\f0\b formed tourist track for Sublime Point Lookout
\f1\b0 . The cliff suddenly stops being an obstacle and becomes ground beneath their boots. Open sandstone, low heath and eucalypt woodland replace the fern gullies, and a few minutes farther on there are constructed paths and lookout infrastructure. From the lookout the Jamison Valley spreads out beneath them, with Mount Solitary, Kings Tableland, Narrow Neck, Ruined Castle and the Three Sisters all visible in their respective directions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hikingtheworld.blog/2023/04/14/lindeman-pass-copeland-pass/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Hiking the World}}\
